ame>Kwee</surname><given-names>RM</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Multimodality imaging of carotid artery plaques: 18F-fluoro-2-deoxyglucose positron emission tomography, computed tomography, and magnetic resonance imaging</article-title><source>Stroke J. Cereb. Circ.</source><year>2009</year><volume>40</volume><fpage>3718</fpage><lpage>3724</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1161/strokeaha.109.564088</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="CR17"><label>17.</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Brinjikji</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Contemporary carotid imaging: From degree of stenosis to plaque vulnerability</article-title><source>J. Neurosurg.</source><year>2016</year><volume>124</volume><fpage>27</fpage><lpage>42</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.3171/2015.1.Jns142452</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">26230478</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="CR18"><label>18.</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Saba</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>CT attenuation analysis of carotid intraplaque hemorrhage</article-title><source>Am. J. Neuroradiol.</source><year>2018</year><volume>39</volume><fpage>131</fpage><lpage>137</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.3174/ajnr.A5461</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">29191874</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="CR19"><label>19.</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Deng</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>The differentiation in image post-processing and 3D reconstruction during evaluation of carotid plaques from MR and CT data sources</article-title><source>Front. Physiol.</source><year>2021</year><volume>12</volume><fpage>645438</fpage><pub-id pu